WEBVTT

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:14.840
Let's go play cops and robbers
at the Whale Park!

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:15.840
Okay!

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:16.470
--All right!

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.390
--They're still playing cops
and robbers as fifth graders.
--All right!

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.220
--They're still playing cops
and robbers as fifth graders.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:22.020
Boys are so childish.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.310
Hey, Futaba. Let's paint this color
on our nails in my room.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:30.110
S-Sure.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:31.530
All right!

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.450
Sorry to keep you waiting. Let's go.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.990
Sure.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:54.720
<i>I had dropped something important</i>
<i>and even though I didn't know you,</i>

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:00.260
<i>You had found it and brought it back</i>
<i>to me unexpectedly this morning</i>

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:06.020
<i>Oh yeah, I was always told to</i>
<i>write my name on important things</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:11.780
<i>Or I might end up losing them somewhere</i>

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.740
<i>It's not (anyone's fault)</i>

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.450
<i>It's not (like it belongs to anyone else)</i>

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:22.660
<i>The world will always be right there</i>

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.370
<i>Let the wind (take you by the hand)</i>

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.170
<i>And the sky (now, breathe together)</i>

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.840
<i>And let's go (it's now begun to move)</i>

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.010
<i>The arrow in our hearts</i>

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:36.930
<i>If I'm (yes, if I'm with you)</i>

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:40.300
<i>With you (yes, because I'm with you)</i>

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:50.480
<i>We still don't know what's going to</i>
<i>happen in this future that's moving forward</i>

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.190
<i>And bouncing glitteringly</i>

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:11.040
"Episode 5"
"Together Again"

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.880
Daddy, I want to go on the boat, too!

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:20.050
Koi said she went on a boat
with her daddy! I wanna go, too!

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:22.640
Hm...

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.180
Why don't you take her fishing
on a boat the next time you're off?

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.690
They'll let grade-school
kids on, won't they?

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:31.060
But Hiyori's the smallest in her class!

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.690
What if she gets thrown out to sea
the moment the boat shakes?!

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:36.820
You are way too overprotective.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.280
I know!

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:41.870
I can just put glue on
the bottom of my feet!

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:45.120
I don't think you'll be able
to fish that way. You sure?

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.120
Let's see...

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.590
Maybe I'll take you when
you're in middle school, Hiyori.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.340
Really? You promise?

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.090
Yup. I promise.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.920
Don't break your promise!

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.800
Hiyori.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.390
Hiyori.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.850
We're almost there.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:14.110
Oh, I'm sorry. I must've fallen asleep.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.980
It's totally fine.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:19.780
You were excited to go bait fishing for
the first time that you couldn't sleep.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:22.780
Th-That's not it!

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:25.950
It's Ichika.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.950
Good morning.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:30.040
Good morning!

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.460
I'm jealous.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:34.750
What? You're not comin', Mr. Yoshinaga?

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:38.710
Dad's going to get interviewed for some
fishing magazine, so he's just our ride.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:42.380
An interview? That's awesome!

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.220
I wanna go fishing, too.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.350
What?

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:47.350
I'm gonna turn down the interview!
I wanna go fishing!

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.100
Do your damn job.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.810
Okay, Hiyori and Koharu!
Make sure you catch plenty for me, too!

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:55.060
Thank you very much.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.900
Honestly.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.360
You're such an entertaining family.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:04.200
Futaba!

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.450
Morning!

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:07.280
Good morning.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:12.120
Are you helping out? What a good girl!

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:15.000
That's not true.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.460
Um... I'm sorry about the other day.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.760
I shouldn't have said something so weird.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:27.180
Aren't you embarrassed to
be fishing when you're a girl?

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.470
Oh, don't even worry about it.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.810
Um... The receptionist desk is inside.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:34.890
Thanks.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:36.600
Let's go, Hiyori.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.610
S-Sure.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.830
Well? Do I look cute?

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.710
You do, but...

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.920
You're gonna be crying later
with that much skin showing.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.710
That voice!

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.090
Who are you?!

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:06.130
What?

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:07.800
No, really! Who are you?!

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.350
It's me, it's me.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:11.770
You're like completely covered up!

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:15.140
Well, of course I am.
I don't want to get sunburnt.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:18.230
Well, I've got sunscreen on,
so I'll be fine.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.110
Not to mention...

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:22.860
We're going to be on a boat
in the ocean in the summer!

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.570
It'd be a waste if you
didn't set yourself free!

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:27.490
Okay, okay, I get it. Jeez.

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:28.820
Koharu!

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:30.160
Coming!

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.080
Be careful.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:32.910
Will it shake?

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:34.910
It'll be fine.

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.460
I'm on a boat!

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.710
You're totally overreacting.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.220
What's wrong, Yamahi?

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:53.560
Oh, uh, um...

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:56.060
Oh, it's nothing.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:57.770
Okay, then.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:01.270
Hey, Koi.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:04.820
I just happened to run into
Futaba in town the other day.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:09.610
And she asked me, "Aren't you embarrassed
to be fishing when you're a girl?"

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.070
Ah...

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:14.290
It is okay for girls to fish, right?

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:17.870
I mean, I know it's not common, but...

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:19.960
You're totally fine.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:24.300
So are you worried about Futaba now?

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.920
Well... that's part of it.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:31.890
But I never properly
answered her question,

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:34.850
so that's been on my mind.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:39.060
Here's your chum.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.150
Chum?

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:43.110
You scatter it into the water
to lure in the fish.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:45.980
We used minced sardines for our chum.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:48.240
Sardines?

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.860
I wonder if you can eat this.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:53.030
How do you use this?

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:56.700
Once you put the chum in there,
you set up your rig.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.330
Rig?

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.420
Ichika.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:03.380
Is there still room on the boat?

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:05.460
Yeah, there is.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:08.880
What? You gonna bring
Mr. Yoshinaga along after all?

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:13.640
Yeah, no. I was wondering
if Futaba could come along.

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:14.930
Futaba?

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:20.640
I haven't been bait fishing since
my dad took me when I was little,

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:25.480
so it's a bit rough having two
bait-fishing newbies tagging along.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:26.780
"Me?"
Me?

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:31.530
So I was hoping I could
have someone help me out.

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.110
You got it.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:39.750
I've come to help out.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.210
It's a pleasure to assist you today.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:45.130
I-It's a pleasure having you on board.

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:48.300
Okay, we're gonna head out in a few.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.300
Aye, aye, sir!

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.430
It feels like our journey's
about to begin!

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:57.970
We're gonna be back in a few hours though.

00:07:57.970 --> 00:08:00.810
Would you like to get ready
before we get to our destination?

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:01.690
Sure.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:05.310
In that case, let's put
the chum in the chum cage.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.520
This?

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:10.860
Yes. If you stuff it too full,
it won't come out very well,

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:13.530
so maybe about 80% full.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.240
How does this look?

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:19.700
I think that's fine.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.290
Next, put the rig you got
at the receptionist desk

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:24.710
in front of the spreader.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.380
As for the bait for the hooks,

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:29.880
we'll be using the eunicid worms
my sister were handing out.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:40.140
Th-Those things bite, right?

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:44.690
Huh? Well, you'll be fine if you
put them on your hook immediately.

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:53.280
Hyah!

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.110
Hyah?

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:55.910
Yo! Yo!

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:04.000
H-Hiyori, are you...?

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:09.710
The other reason
I only ever do fly fishing...

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:13.210
I can't touch bugs.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.180
That's so pathetic, Hiyori.

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:17.800
That's gross! Go away!

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:20.350
It's sorta surprising that
Koharu's handling this better.

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:22.220
They're like the grunt
characters that appear

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:24.180
in action-horror games. They're cute.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.440
They're not cute at all!

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:29.310
I just got laughed at...

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:32.280
Oh! I-I'm so sorry!

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:37.200
Um... I don't mind
getting the bait on for you.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.240
Th-Thanks.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.870
Good for you, Hiyori.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:48.670
Okay, try fishing around here.
Two meters from there.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:50.630
Go ahead and dunk the rig in.

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:52.000
We're not going to cast it?

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.010
Nope. You just drop it in.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:01.260
Th-The line just keeps going,
but where do I stop it?

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.560
It'll stop on its own
when it reaches the bottom.

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:08.310
When it hits the bottom,
reel the line in about two meters.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:12.070
Pull up the rod a bit
so the chum can spread out.

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:13.610
Hup.

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:15.690
Spin the reel once.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.610
Wait about 20 to 30 seconds for the

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:20.240
horse mackerel to be hooked
after being lured in by the chum.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.780
If nothing happens,

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:26.250
try dropping it to the bottom again
and repeat what followed.

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:31.380
Something feels weird.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:33.960
Maybe you got a bite.
Try reeling in your line.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:38.630
Oh, right. This is
different from fly fishing.

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:40.930
This spinny thing makes me
feel like I'm really fishing!

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:43.510
Fly fishing is really fishing, too!

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:47.430
Horse mackerel, huh?
I wonder how I should prepare them.

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:50.150
We deep fried them last time,

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:55.900
so I guess we could have sashimi
or maybe the <i>namero </i>Dad likes.

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:58.360
Who's this?!

00:10:58.360 --> 00:10:59.450
That's a scorpionfish.

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:02.160
Scorpionfish?! The poisonous ones?

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.910
Hairy stingfish are.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:07.290
It's pretty rare to catch a scorpionfish.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:09.620
It's rare? Like super rare?

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:11.710
Well, they're rockfish.

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:12.420
"Rockabye Baby Fish"

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:12.420
Well, they're rockfish.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:15.000
"Rockabye Baby Fish"

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:15.000
What are rockabye baby fish?

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.710
"Rockabye Baby Fish"

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.710
You've got the wrong idea.
This is how its written.

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:19.720
You've got the wrong idea.
This is how its written.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:24.350
They're fish that usually hang out
among the reefs and seaweed.

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:28.220
Which probably means
your bait was too far down.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.690
Are you trying to say that I suck?

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:33.310
They taste good, so it's fine.

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:39.530
I think... I got a bite!

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:45.830
What a huge haul!

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:48.240
You can catch so much
when you're bait fishing!

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:51.870
I need to show off to
our parents when we get home.

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:55.340
Koharu, did you enjoy
this more than fly fishing?

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:59.960
Th-That's not true!
Fly fishing is fun, too!

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:02.680
You must all really like fishing.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:05.140
We do! Even if we were
stranded on some island,

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:07.640
we can survive if we know how to fish.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:09.470
Even a deserted island!

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:12.810
That's what you're thinking
about when you're fishing?

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:16.060
And today was my first time
on a boat but it was so much fun!

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:17.440
I can't wait to go again.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:18.980
Yeah.

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:25.160
Oh, yeah. Why don't we all get together
and eat the fish we caught today?

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:27.700
I'd like to thank you and Ichika, too.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:28.580
Huh?

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:30.000
Yeah, that's a great idea.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.540
Then I guess we should get
this horse mackerel party started!

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:32.790
"Tsurifuku"

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:32.790
Then I guess we should get
this horse mackerel party started!

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:34.750
"Tsurifuku"

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:34.750
You really do love parties.

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:36.170
"Tsurifuku"

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:36.170
I do!

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:37.000
"Tsurifuku"

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:44.930
I would always play outside on my breaks.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:48.720
The other girls would always
stay inside and trade stickers,

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:52.100
or make something with beads.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:57.770
But I would always be outside
with the boys playing tag or soccer.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:03.240
It was just... I liked
playing outside more.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:07.240
Futaba! Can I come over
to your place on Sunday?

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:08.830
Show me how to fish!

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:09.990
Me, too!

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.700
Sure!

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:18.170
I never even considered how
that might look to the other kids.

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:21.170
--Yay!

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:22.260
--Niji, Tora, sit down!
--Yay!

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.630
--Niji, Tora, sit down!
--Party!

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:24.090
--Party!

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:25.930
--I'm sorry they're so noisy.
--Party!

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:29.260
It's fine. They're making
the room very lively and fun.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:31.640
Okay, let's get cooking.

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:33.810
I hope you'll show me the ropes.

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:36.190
What should I do?

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:39.360
Could you cut the veggies we need
for the salad with Hiyori then?

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.230
Got it.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:43.490
We're going to make <i>namero</i>.

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:44.900
Okay.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:49.660
First, we're going to finely chop
some green onions and some ginger.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:54.830
Next, we're going to slice up the
horse mackerel we already filleted.

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.500
Then we'll top that with the
green onions, ginger, and miso,

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:00.920
then you're going to chop it all up
even finer as you also mixed it together.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.500
Like this?

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:05.670
Yes! Make sure you mix
everything up every now and then,

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:08.760
and once it becomes a
smooth texture, you're finished.

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:10.010
Like this?

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:12.260
That looks great!

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:14.140
Let's give it a taste.

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:20.520
It's so good!

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:23.860
And now, for one more dish.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:25.280
With the spine?

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:29.070
I usually throw it away, but then,
Ichika showed me something.

