then use a paper towel
to wipe off all the moisture.

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:37.120
"Starch"

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:37.120
then use a paper towel
to wipe off all the moisture.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.120
"Starch"

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.120
Throw on some starch,

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:39.500
Throw on some starch,

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:43.040
deep fry it in oil at a
low temperature for a while,

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:46.420
and then raise the temperature really
quickly at the end to make it crisp.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:50.430
That looks delicious!

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:52.050
Why don't we have a little taste?

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:53.680
Sure.

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:58.640
It's so good!

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:01.480
A star!

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:04.320
You did a great job. Thank you.

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:05.980
I made a fishy!

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:07.990
Hey, pay attention.

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:09.320
Ta-dah!

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:12.320
The Yoshinaga family specialty:
horse mackerel hamburgers!

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:13.830
Look forward to it.

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:17.790
Dad, that's too big, and won't cook right.

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:19.330
Oh, really?

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:22.830
Hayato, you know a lot
more about cooking now.

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:25.130
Sis taught me well.

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:38.270
It's been so long since
our house was this lively.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:42.400
Everyone used to always
gather at our house like this

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:45.110
and we'd eat together.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:47.860
But now...

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:52.160
I can't cook well enough
to invite people over!

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:56.450
So...

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.540
Thank you.

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:02.620
I would love to keep
cooking with you like this.

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:05.380
Of course!

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:11.260
I wonder if Ichika and Futaba are here.

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:13.590
Yeah, I'll go take a look.

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:20.600
Hiyori's usually so shy,
but she's willingly going to the door?

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:23.650
Maybe it's because of her new job.

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:26.020
I see.

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:27.360
I'm back.

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:29.070
Thanks for having us over!

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:30.530
It's great to have you.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:34.110
I'm sorry. We were changing
and lost track of time.

00:16:34.110 --> 00:16:36.160
Here. We bought a cake as a gift.

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:38.540
Thank you so much!

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:42.250
Futaba insisted that we bring a gift.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:46.540
She's so much more responsible than I am!

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:51.460
Ichika, Futaba, dinner's basically ready.

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:54.930
<i>Namero</i>!

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:57.010
We have some saké,
so make sure you have some.

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:58.760
Heck yeah!

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:01.770
Oh, wait. I can't. I have to drive.

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:04.020
I can drive us home.

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:05.440
Really? Yay!

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:07.230
Yay!

00:17:10.190 --> 00:17:11.530
It's so pretty.

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:16.280
The stuff on top is Japanese-style gelée.
Isn't it all nice and sparkly?

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:18.740
Let's eat!

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:25.500
I thought this when I tasted it earlier,
but this horse mackerel is so good.

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:28.960
Yes. The horse mackerel
we caught today is called "kinaji."

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:30.090
Like gold?!

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:33.510
They don't migrate, so they stay in
the same spot and eat a lot of food,

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:37.390
so they end up really fatty and delicious.

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:40.850
So this horse mackerel is basically
like some Roman emperor...

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:44.140
They get damaged when you
catch a lot in a net at once,

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:47.020
so this is something special that
people who go fishing get to enjoy.

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:51.440
How the heck am I supposed to go
back to store-bought fish after this?

00:17:55.860 --> 00:18:01.240
Lately, I started remembering
I can have fun outside of fishing, too.

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:04.910
When I was little, I would bring
the fish I caught back home,

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:08.040
and my dad would cook it.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:11.130
My mom would look so happy
and say it's delicious,

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:14.130
and we'd all be smiling.

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:15.590
That's why...

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:26.180
Th-That's why...

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:31.770
It's not embarrassing
to go fishing... at all.

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:37.320
I-I'm so sorry! I didn't... um...

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:41.870
I wasn't saying that
people who fish are weird.

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:44.080
Um...

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:47.120
Someone from my class told me

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:52.670
that it was weird for me to do
things boys enjoy when I'm a girl.

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:56.510
They were saying I was just
doing it because I liked the boys.

00:18:57.720 --> 00:19:00.340
Because you liked the boys?

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:07.520
That's why I stopped
playing with the boys.

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:11.690
Because I found out
I sort of stood out in class.

00:19:11.690 --> 00:19:17.070
But you also fish because
that's what your family does.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:20.360
I don't think anyone would think
you're weird for having it as a hobby.

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:27.120
Yeah! And Ichika is also a lady, and
is a captain, and is super awesome!

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:30.250
Well, my sister is special.

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:36.050
My sister is always
so confident, charming,

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:38.380
and loved by everyone.

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:50.440
But I... If I'm not like everyone else,

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:52.900
they'll all hate me.

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:03.490
Futaba...

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:13.630
Is that why you stopped fishing?! Futaba!

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:15.750
She cries when she's drunk?

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:23.390
Don't say people hate you!
Your big sister loves you so much!

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:34.600
Sis, you smell like alcohol.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:44.160
Yeah... I'm good.

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:49.540
Futaba...

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:51.290
Thank you for having us over.

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:53.710
Futaba, come over again, okay?

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:54.960
I will.

00:20:57.630 --> 00:20:59.750
Okay, let's get cleaning.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:00.960
Sure.

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:09.350
...that it was weird for me to do
things boys enjoy when I'm a girl.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.230
Okay, let's go.

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:16.190
Thank you for driving us.

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:23.990
H-Hey.

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:26.320
Hiyori?

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:32.500
Futaba, would you...

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:36.290
...b-be friends with me?

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:40.960
Um, I...

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:44.720
It's fun fishing alone,

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:49.390
but fishing with your
friends, um, is fun, too.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:55.890
Let's go fishing together again.

00:21:55.890 --> 00:21:59.610
Next time, you should hold a rod, too.

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:15.790
Okay.

00:22:20.290 --> 00:22:24.050
Together... again.

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:32.810
<i>Even if you don't say anything</i>

00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:38.560
<i>I know how you're feeling and</i>
<i>when you're lying or telling the truth</i>

00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:41.190
<i>Even if you don't do anything</i>

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:46.190
<i>Just being next to you</i>
<i>makes the day brighter</i>

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:50.410
<i>The reason I've always loved the ocean</i>

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:55.160
<i>Is because you were always by my side</i>

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:58.370
<i>The way we laugh is becoming similar</i>

00:22:58.370 --> 00:23:03.500
<i>It's almost like we're cider</i>

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:07.720
<i>Bubble, bubble, our laughter combines</i>

00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:12.010
<i>Bubble, bubble, then floats up</i>
<i>and pops together</i>

00:23:12.010 --> 00:23:20.270
<i>We gather up the light and</i>
<i>gain even more precious things</i>

00:23:20.270 --> 00:23:24.520
<i>Bubble, bubble, our laughter combines</i>

00:23:24.520 --> 00:23:28.860
<i>Bubble, bubble, then floats up</i>
<i>and pops together</i>

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:33.830
<i>May a present where we can</i>
<i>laugh about the past and future</i>

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:39.960
<i>Always be right here</i>

00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:46.500
<i>May a present where we can</i>
<i>laugh about the past and future</i>

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:52.890
<i>Always be right here</i>

00:23:55.010 --> 00:23:55.890
"Next Time"

00:23:55.890 --> 00:23:59.270
"Next Time"
What do you need to always
remember when you're on a boat?

00:23:59.270 --> 00:24:01.060
"Next Time"
A liberating sense of fashion!

00:24:01.060 --> 00:24:02.650
"Next Time"
You've gotta look cute!

00:24:02.650 --> 00:24:05.520
"Next Time"
Yes, of course.
Cuteness is life. Wait, no!

00:24:05.520 --> 00:24:06.730
"Next Time"
You need a life jacket!

00:24:06.730 --> 00:24:09.860
"Next Time"
We could start a comedy duo.
